 # Existing JSON utility
 
-Use `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin. Existing action: length. Domain functions accept the payload object; api.dispatch routes it. CLI reports ValueError/KeyError with stderr and exit 2.
+Use `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin. Domain functions accept the payload object; api.dispatch routes it. CLI reports ValueError/KeyError with stderr and exit 2.
+
+Actions:
+- `length`: payload `{"action":"length","text":...}`; returns Python code-point length of `text`.
+- `index`: payload `{"action":"index","text":...,"byte_offsets":[int,...]}`; returns `{"byte_length":int,"char_to_byte":[int,...],"byte_to_char":[int,...]}`. `char_to_byte` has `len(text)+1` cumulative UTF-8 byte offsets (starting 0, including the end). `byte_to_char` maps each requested byte offset to its code-point index, preserving request order/repetitions. The end offset is valid and maps to `len(text)`; empty text has boundaries `[0]`. Raises ValueError if any requested offset is negative, beyond the encoded byte length, or inside a multi-byte code point. Code-point indices only: no normalization, case conversion or grapheme segmentation.
